# Backlog — planned tasks not yet started

> The coordinator's **cross-session todo list**. The in-chat plan (task
> breakdown, merges, priorities) lives only in a coordinator session and is lost
> when that session is replaced — this file is where it survives. Each entry is a
> task that has been planned/scoped but does **not yet** have a brief in
> `.harness/active/` (briefs are the next stage; this is the stage before them).
>
> **Coordinator contract:**
> - On startup, read this file. If it has queued items, present them to the user
>   with a recommended order and ask which to start first — only open that brief
>   after the user confirms. If it's empty, proceed normally (ask what they want).
> - Whenever you plan, split, merge, or reprioritise tasks, write them here.
> - When a brief is created for a queued item, remove it from "Queued" (it now
>   lives in `.harness/active/`).
>
> This is unrelated to the CONTRIBUTING `🛠 TODO` gate.

